body:
Several method signatures in this snippet don’t match the current SDK (e.g. `auth.refreshToken` takes a string, not an object; `permissions.getEffectivePermissions` takes no object argument). Please align these examples with `packages/client/src/index.ts` so they compile/copy-paste cleanly.
```suggestion
await client.auth.refreshToken('token');

// Permissions — Access control checks
await client.permissions.check({ object: 'account', action: 'create' });
await client.permissions.getObjectPermissions('account');
await client.permissions.getEffectivePermissions();
```

These examples don’t match the current SDK API shapes: `automation.trigger` is not called with `{ trigger, payload }`, `storage.upload` / `getDownloadUrl` aren’t options-object based, and `views.*` methods require an `object` argument (and different parameter ordering). Please update the examples to match the actual signatures.
```suggestion
await client.automation.trigger('send_welcome_email', { userId });

// Storage — File upload and management
await client.storage.upload(fileData, 'account', 'logo');
await client.storage.getDownloadUrl('file-123');

// Views — UI view management
await client.views.list('account');
await client.views.get('account', viewId);
await client.views.create('account', { name: 'my_view', ... });
await client.views.update('account', viewId, { ... });
await client.views.delete('account', viewId);
```

`client.packages.install({ packageId: ... })` doesn’t match the current SDK API (the implementation expects a manifest payload, not a packageId). Update this example to reflect the actual method signature.
```suggestion
await client.packages.install({
  name: 'vendor_plugin',
  label: 'Vendor Plugin',
  version: '1.0.0',
});
```

These examples reference methods/signatures that don’t exist in the current SDK (`client.analytics.getMeta`) and use an automation trigger signature that doesn’t match the implementation. Please align the README examples with `packages/client/src/index.ts` (e.g. `client.analytics.meta(cube)` and the actual `automation.trigger` parameters).
```suggestion
await client.analytics.meta('sales');

// Automation
await client.automation.trigger('send_welcome_email', { userId });
```

Storage examples here don’t match the current SDK API (`storage.upload` and `getDownloadUrl` take positional arguments in the implementation, not an options object). Update these to the actual method signatures so the snippet is runnable.
```suggestion
await client.storage.upload(fileData, 'contact', 'avatar');
await client.storage.getDownloadUrl('file-123');
```
